RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Measurement profile: recorded scorer mechanics, split origins, class drift, cold rates, warm-history ages, and team-size tail in eval_profile.md.
Evaluation suite: left immutable; the registered kapso_evaluation/kapso_eval.py remains the evaluation entrypoint.
Recovered issue: the first debug build failed because sanitized citations contain nullable referenced paper IDs; citation-event construction now filters missing foreign keys before integer indexing.
Full run run_0003: binary shared scorer selected on two expanding origins; 200 rounds, four-year seed half-life, and no prior correction scored 0.535922081250801 validation accuracy.
Feature widening after run_0003: added explicit non-overlapping history windows, share momentum, recent coauthor affinity, multi-scale causal Author_ID neighborhood priors, and distance beyond the observed author frontier.
Full run run_0007: widened model scored 0.5363834422657952; internal mean was statistically tied but slightly lower, so the next revision addresses the discovered forward-fold availability bug and adds explicitly causal outcome-prior features.
Recovered issue: internal expanding folds had selected rows by seed date rather than label-availability date, allowing targets whose windows had not closed at the simulated origin; fold training and prior estimation now require seed date plus 182 days to be at or before the origin.
Recovered issue: checkpoint selection considered only 200-600 rounds even though both forward folds often peaked at 50-150; checkpoint aggregation now covers 50, 100, 150, 200, 300, 400, 500, and 600 rounds.
Full run run_0010: causal fold selection chose binary loss, 50 rounds, four-year recency, and no label-shift exponent, scoring 0.5367166474432911. The latest internal fold measured 0.71736 warm accuracy but only 0.05641 cold accuracy, identifying cold prediction as the current score bound.
Cold feature widening: added a causal recent cold-outcome prior and an internally gated cold fallback; it is enabled only if replacing ranker scores on cold rows improves both expanding train-only origins.
Recovered issue: the first cold fallback used only the most recent available origin, whose leading class was unstable and achieved 0.02298 on the earlier internal fold. A causal pooled cold prior measured 0.08341 and 0.08190 on the two latest internal origins, so cold fallback now uses the stable pooled distribution and remains gated on both folds.
Full run run_0013: the pooled cold fallback improved the registered validation accuracy to 0.547763680635653 and was selected because it improved both causal forward folds.
Cold name model: a 120,000-feature character TF-IDF SGD classifier trained only on labels available at each origin scored 0.09174 and 0.08808 on the last two internal cold cohorts, exceeding the pooled prior on both; the separate Model A and Model B cold chains are now internally gated.
Cold name calibration: train-only comparison of loss, regularization, and prior tempering selected log-loss alpha 1e-4 plus one pooled-prior logit, scoring 0.09287 and 0.08950 on the two latest cold origins.
Warm affinity blend: added an expanding-fold gate over small bonuses for the cheap decayed-affinity winner, retaining a blend only when warm accuracy improves at every usable origin.
Transition feature widening: added categorical career-top/candidate, recent-top/candidate, and last-category/candidate interaction IDs so the shared scorer can learn category-specific persistence and switching rules without separate per-class trees.
Transition interaction result: TESTED-REJECTED after internal objective mean fell from about 0.5157 to 0.5127 and warm accuracy also declined; the three high-cardinality interactions were removed before final evaluation.
